{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar","id":860086,"title":"Four Werewolves walk into a bar.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-05T20:51:33-07:00","id":860086,"title":"Four Werewolves walk into a bar.","content":"Title unrelated.<br /> So I'm going to be running Werewolf 2nd ed since my group wanted to play something other than Demon; I've been running the Descent since it came out.<br /> Anyways. All those years games of Demon and I'm not really sure how to do Werewolf?<br /> I understand the core concept of the game I've read the Core for both 1st and 2nd edition. But clearly Werewolf is nothing like Demon. <br /> So a few things.<br /> Is it Closer to Monster of the Week or can a hunt take chapters worth of doing and then final out with &quot;The Big hunt&quot;<br /> <br /> Since werewolves have to protect their territory, It's not so easy as a claimed comes around and blows stuff up right? Problems begin gradually (because of course they do) and then if ignored or can't be solved soon enough stuff goes to hell. Standard progression right?<br /> <br /> Spirits and the Shadow. Exactly how close to our world does the Shadow appear to our world? A 100% copy or is it a little more abstract? As far as spirits go, can this game function without Technology spirits? Do they have to be a thing because I just don't get them. I understand Virtue, Vice, Conceptual, elemental, Emotional spirits. But I don't understand the point or need for a spirit that is a boat, car, or city with out finding the idea humorous (Do you actually walk into a spirit that is Spokane Washington or yell at it from the top of a Spirit Mountain?) For that matter what about a blade of grass, most spirits or slumbering but don't those slumbering spirits get eaten by the spirit of the lawn or the Pride spirit that feeds of the man who owns the yard, does it further eat the house spirit that was asleep before the man turned into a home and now exists only to bolster that pride, house, and lawn? <br /> <br /> A little less head hurting. I only have 4 players, Do we need a 5th? Should all four tribes be reflected in the pack? How common are other packs/ tribes/ roving packs of The People?<br /> <br /> I'm on my 2nd read through to get ready for Werewolf. I read and the imagery it conveys is great. But at the same time I can't help but feel I'm woefully not prepared to do this with only having Demon the Descent and Geist the Sin-eaters under my belt. <br /> <br /> So any advice any of you could offer. what your first stories were like and so forth. That would just be great.<br /> (I literally created my user I.D. again after years of just lurking to ask these questions)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T21:20:49-07:00","id":860101,"title":"","content":"Hunts are a question of how &quot;important&quot; you want to emphasize a certain prey or how important an objective is. If something's really big, really epic, give it a larger story to compensate that is more than just a single session. Think of it like a... Quest. A real one. Where the journey itself is an objective to enjoy.<br /> <br /> Less important hunts <i>can </i>be Monster of the Week though and that option is available if you want it.<br /> <br /> 4 players is fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways. Blades of grass are too small and unimportant to make an &quot;awake&quot; spirit, though they possess a reflection. The entire field might be a weak spirit though.<br /> <br /> As for Technology and City spirits; everything except humans that exists has a spiritual reflection. Removing them would create a bit of a plot hole or an excusion wouldn't it? As for handling them, I recall hearing about this once scene in one of the books about a City Spirit represented by well, a queen or a king bringing a werewolf towards it... just to make it clear who's top dog in some sort of godfather-eque sequence. To me, the City spirit is not just the city itself, not just its very &quot;identity&quot; , but also its ruler.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, unless we're talking about really important or really value items, such as say... the Titanic's spirit or the Hope Diamonds, most item spirits should be fairly weak and low on the totem pole.... Powerful item spirits often might not represent single items, but rather entire collections or even networks of such... Let's say for example the difference between a low rank Computer spirit and uh... Whispering Watcher, the Master Administrator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-06-2016, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T21:23:46-07:00","id":860103,"title":"","content":"Welp, you've got a lot of concerns. This is how I tackle them in my own games:<br /> <br /> 1) You can do Monster of the Week or progress thru a Big Bad, The Wolf Must Hunt means that Uratha will engage in Sacred Hunts regularly. The Big Bad progression is usually a progression of sacred hunts.<br /> <br /> 2) Uratha prefer to be the apex predators in their turfs. It's less about &quot;protecting&quot; is more about dictating how it would develop. A pack which thrives on members of the homeless population will have quite a different outlook and notion of what is good for a territory of white-collar universe graduates who do the corporate conga.<br /> <br /> 3) Think of the Shadow as the subconscious of the world. The more symbolic weight something has, the easier it is for it to manifest. A recently opened pops shop will have a negligible impact in the Shadow compared to the two decades old Walmart that completely shifted the economy in the town. The more dramatic something is, the higher the chance for it to manifest spiritually.<br /> <br /> 4) Technology spirits aren't the same as transport ones (such as computer spirits). Consider that most spirits are shaken awake from traumatic events, such as having their reflection destroyed (or heavily damaged); most cars you'll see in the Shadow are mere reflections, moving above their physical reflections without any display of sentience. The same is true for that ferry. Yes, there can be traffic jams in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> 5) The bigger a spirit is, the harder it is that it'll just manifest into a single form. This is true to mountain spirits, to city spirits, to country spirits or to spirits of whole seas. At any rate they're unimportant, unless something shocks them awake.<br /> <br /> 6) A blade of grass will manifest spiritually as long as it makes coherent sense in the place in question. If the place is a park? Sure. If it's was just planted besides a Starbucks? doubt it.<br /> <br /> 7) There's 5 tribes, actually, not 4. If you want to know how many Uratha there are in some metropolitan area? Take it's population and the 1% of it will be it. Divide as you might in between Forsaken &amp; Pure. Adjust the figure accordingly to story needs.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks\">Here's a thread with storyseeds for Forsaken.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T21:25:04-07:00","id":860104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar#post860086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits and the Shadow. Exactly how close to our world does the Shadow appear to our world? A 100% copy or is it a little more abstract?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, the lower the Gauntlet rating the less abstract the Shadow looks in a given area. This means cities tend to look pretty weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as spirits go, can this game function without Technology spirits? Do they have to be a thing because I just don't get them. I understand Virtue, Vice, Conceptual, elemental, Emotional spirits. But I don't understand the point or need for a spirit that is a boat, car, or city with out finding the idea humorous </div> </div> </div>The Artificial choirs are important because they represent as near to an additive ephemeral footprint as mankind can have on the Shadow without leaning into temporary and overdriven stuff like emotional spirits.<br /> <br /> Unless your mind immediately goes to cartoony shenanigans I'm not seeing a disproportionate amount of inherent humor in the notion that the scraps of intelligence supported by the care and attention your car receives are inclined to try to grow through that channel and branch out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For that matter what about a blade of grass, most spirits or slumbering but don't those slumbering spirits get eaten by the spirit of the lawn or the Pride spirit that feeds of the man who owns the yard, does it further eat the house spirit that was asleep before the man turned into a home and now exists only to bolster that pride, house, and lawn? </div> </div> </div>Low-Rank spirits aren't terribly imaginative in terms of what is and isn't food and higher-Rank spirits tend to recognize the value of letting their lessers grow out of inherent dormancy. The boundaries between spirits tend to hold up fairly well until they start getting greedy or desperate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-06-2016, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T21:45:58-07:00","id":860118,"title":"","content":"So why does a human really liking a car wake up a car spirit? That's the technology thing I don't get. I have a car. It runs and I take it to the shop when the engine light goes on. But I don't think it had a personality or can do favors for someone. <br /> <br /> I mean unless the idea behind a technology spirit is more along the line of a way of describing the sheer source of power that humans are. <br /> <br /> Like humanity creates such a large splattering of essence that it wakes a sort of spirit that never was. I mean okay that I can get. Kinda. But maybe I'm to detached from machines being tools and my city a place I live. <br /> <br /> I think I have a general idea as far as everything else goes. But if one of my players doesn't pick a storm lord should I just omit their preferred prey?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T21:59:08-07:00","id":860121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar?p=860118#post860118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why does a human really liking a car wake up a car spirit? That's the technology thing I don't get. I have a car. It runs and I take it to the shop when the engine light goes on. But I don't think it had a personality or can do favors for someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the car that would have a personality, the spirit would, and even then only if it was a certain Rank. But lets say you took very good care of your car, maybe even had it uniquely detailed. All that time and energy and thought you've spent on your car might awaken it. The car might inspire envy in others, it's a trophy, an spirit of pride and beauty. Maybe you drag race, and constantly enhance your car, or it's become known on the circuit. The car's spirit growls in the Hisil, wanting to race, to be the fastest thing around. Maybe someone was the victim of a hit and run, the details of the car are all over the news but the person is never caught, the car is never tracked down. The car might awaken, with an influence of Fear or Mystery. It might just be a Fear spirit that looks like the car.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like humanity creates such a large splattering of essence that it wakes a sort of spirit that never was. I mean okay that I can get. Kinda. But maybe I'm to detached from machines being tools and my city a place I live. </div> </div> </div>Cities have spirits, usually old, sometimes really powerful or not as powerful as they once were. Just by being a name on the map you give it potential, but all the people who've lived there and call the place home, who work there for the city, repairing it or protecting it add to it. It might sit in city hall, a harried bureaucrat keeping things in order and being offered tithes of Essence by all the minor spirits that make up the city. It might be a broken down capitol building that sparks memories of times when things were better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I have a general idea as far as everything else goes. But if one of my players doesn't pick a storm lord should I just omit their preferred prey? </div> </div> </div>It's not necessary. Each tribe gets a little leg up against their sacred prey but they aren't required to hunt them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T22:18:00-07:00","id":860126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar?p=860118#post860118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why does a human really liking a car wake up a car spirit? That's the technology thing I don't get. I have a car. It runs and I take it to the shop when the engine light goes on. But I don't think it had a personality or can do favors for someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they can be objects of desire? Because their mere presence can immediately guarantee that you'll get lucky tonight?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar?p=860118#post860118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have a general idea as far as everything else goes. But if one of my players doesn't pick a storm lord should I just omit their preferred prey?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't. Why, if I was a spirit that they fucked with and noticed they have no Storm Lord packmate, I'd go out of my way to claim someone and get some sweet, sweet payback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T22:34:35-07:00","id":860131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar?p=860118#post860118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why does a human really liking a car wake up a car spirit? That's the technology thing I don't get. I have a car. It runs and I take it to the shop when the engine light goes on. But I don't think it had a personality or can do favors for someone.<br /> <br /> [\u2026] But maybe I'm to detached from machines being tools and my city a place I live.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have no trouble understanding the concept of emotional spirits and you've got a nominal grasp of the notion that something like &quot;really liking&quot; a car can awaken its spirit, so I'm not sure how being aware that you're not particularly attached to technology in general is an obstacle to making the connection that having that car be a thing that is cared about makes it different from a car that is viewed the way you view your car.<br /> <br /> Most artificial spirits do not awaken naturally if left alone, because in the most basic terms spirits begin as the literal living history of the things that spawned them and on the ground level they interact with the Shadow as an ecosystem. A plain car with no outstanding elements to its history probably won't awaken without spiritual interference or some confluence of events that makes that car or cars as a whole important or significant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T23:04:40-07:00","id":860138,"title":"","content":"Has anyone used a tech spirit in their game? What was it? What was the interaction like l? What kind of gifts can they bestow? Can one be used as a totem,?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T23:33:40-07:00","id":860146,"title":"","content":"They can bestow a wide range of gifts. Technology, obviously. But also Knowledge, Shaping, potentially Warding.<br /> <br /> I had a surveillance-based tech spirit as an ally in one game, it was very useful for inhabiting surveillance cameras and getting me the information on them, as well as wire tapping and pulling info from cell phones. In another game we had a roiling mass of wires and blinking lights &quot;City's Reach&quot; as our pack's totem. Sort of a lovecraftian horror made out of tech. It was cool and terrifying and had a very weird ban that I can't quite remember anymore. It was very well informed on most things, but probably because it was basically the internet.<br /> <br /> Car spirits in my game were terrifying, as they rammed violently any spirits that tried to walk on &quot;their roads.&quot; They ran the Motor City as far as they were concerned. They mowed down a couple of the pack (they had vicious looking mouths on their undercarriage, which the pack cub found out the hard way). They also used the blast numina constantly via their horns, and had the pack bleeding from their eardrums. <br /> <br /> Ford is built tough, man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T01:57:19-07:00","id":860181,"title":"","content":"I found the best way to build Werewolf chronicle is marking one varied enemy in one theme as main games antagonists - like Malejin, Bale Hounds and their spirits - or maybe some last Pangean, Claimed and human cultists - or Pure, their powerful Totems and humans in slavery under them - with a variety smaller &quot;Monsters of the Week&quot; for those not going normally under theme umbrella.<br /> <br /> Think here a bit like <b><i>Supernatural</i></b> TV series - each week you have surely The Hunt, only sometimes they are connected to the main plots seasons arc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:28:39-07:00","id":860244,"title":"","content":"Check out the art on Page 248. That's what technology spirits look like. You're picturing a talking bus or something, right? You should be thinking more along the lines of mechanical monstrosities with churning gears and blades and crap. Bus spirits that eat people. Slaughterhouses and meat packing plants home to vicious horrors made of spinning blades.<br /> <br /> Think Walkerbreaker from Predators, a truck/pain magath that spends it's time running people over. Spirits don't have a <i>purpose</i>. They just exist, and do what they do without any care or restraint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:19:10-07:00","id":860322,"title":"","content":"If you need inspiration for the urban shadow and it's denizens I highly recommend Mr. Shopping's AP Detroit Rock City. It's 1e, and pretty atypical in that the pack gets run off of their territory almost immediately, but it is really good. Detroit is kind of a hell hole and it definitely shows in the shadows, most places probably aren't as bad. There is a link to it, along with a few selections from it at the following link:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=839392#post839392\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...392#post839392</a><br /> <br /> The shadow reflection of a graveyard:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Strange heat...this crackling sensation as you are enveloped by rubbery, fleshy scar-like folds, invisibly drawn in towards the statue, your insides roiling as the heat yields to a wrenching pull, disorienting you badly for a few seconds before you feel yourself being passed through the Gauntlet and spat out on the Other Side, stumbling as you regain your footing in this suddenly alien landscape. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A shadowy mockery of the real world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Twisted monuments rise skyward, distorted with age and strangely slender, like they were being sucked up by an unseen force, others squat and crushed, pulled into the earth until only their stony, slime-pitted tops can be seen. Others lean to the side, slowly sinking into a sea of patchy white snow. Mausoleums are warped this way and that like a Salvador Dali painting, leaking a strange purplish haze. Motes of light lazily dance past, trailing like masses of phosphorescence, bobbing up and down before your eyes. You can feel the solace spirits press in all around you, their aspects little slitted yellow eyes drawn over with transparent fabric to reveal muffled mouths. Silently writhing, calcified maggots worm about in the cold earth, burrowing into the mounds of graves and tops of tombstones - aspects of decay. Winter wights and cold spirits breed incessantly, icy cascades of their reproduction splashing into the strange night air like blue sparks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Luna gazes down from overhead with her Shaman face, cutting the sky in half with her silvery light.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The graveyard stretches from the hill down to a vast river of blood, slowly flowing and cutting like a razor's edge through the earth, a ruddy zig-zag that glows and belches crimson gas. Vague, Pompeii-like bodies calcified with ancient, unidentifiable armor form the banks of this hellish river. At the very horizon are the tall, pointed spikes of a fence that joins with a floating upper half, a mirror image that warps to grin in places like a mouthful of fangs. In the distance you see the winking corpse-lights of Downtown, buildings that stretch miles into the sky even though they are burnt out as if caught in a that massive nuclear blast that defines the Shadow of this place. Only the biting cold is familiar.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Before you is a cold white alabaster angel with torn-off wings, weeping black ooze from her eyes and shorn-away nose, fingers clasped in prayer as she slowly sinks into oblivion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It stinks here. It stinks of decay and moldy stone, enough to make your stomach turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You can hear the sibilant spirit whispers filter from the shadows.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">'Bastard wolves desecrate this place...'</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">'[Why do they run...they run....why...]'</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">'[...Yes, for they fight and eat each other...]'</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Shadow of Detroit.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Detroit Suburbs:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A fair appraisal of tonight, a nightmare ride of blood and fang, trial by fire. The near escapes you'd pulled off could have frayed anyone's nerves raw, but it wasn't over yet. You were still in the Shadow of one of the most dangerous cities in the country, stalking through this darkened, gutted suburb that looked like it had been firebombed over and over until only twisted, skeletal frames remained. Bad memories here - you could feel the eyes of skulking, lurking spirits, hiding amongst fallen rafters and piles of rubble, their eyes flitting in the dark. Aspects of destitution, frustration and broken homes - powerful emotions, thoughts and actions given form on the Other Side. </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You can hear their whispers, like chittering static, white noise that doesn't even make sense in the First Tongue - whatever it is, it\u2019s hateful. Unlike the cold spirits, however, these aren't glutted with the strength of Detroit's savage winter, and don't leave their holes. The chill lessens to a much more bearable degree, though you still see cold wights flitting through the air high above.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Slowly, this ghost town transitions into a gently undulating series of bald hills dotted with gnarled trees that look like corpse hands, branches rubbery and grey-brown, flesh sprouting strange leaves that look like fingernails, slowly oozing black ichor-like sap to patter against the bare ground. The floor sinks slightly with each step, bluish black, like damp clay. The trees grow more and more numerous as you continue, shivering as you approach. Strange insects feed off of the foul sap, bloated abdomens and tiny, shrunken heads that look like they belong to forgotten dolls, eyes blank and glassy, wings buzzing and barely keeping them aloft.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In the distance, you can see a massive copper building that slowly sinks into the clay, the structure dotted with shattered windows that reflect Luna\u2019s light with all the charm of a broken-toothed grin. Another twin structure looms behind it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Jericho, you know these must be Lafayette Towers.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> You can both see the spires of Detroit rising from the cityscape behind Lafayette Towers, squat, blown-out buildings gutted and blackened, like the rotting teeth of a skeleton's lower jaw. Skyscrapers rise drooped as if from a nuclear blast, reminding you of the ribcage of a giant, city-spanning predator. Apocalyptic fires still dot here and there, burning like a thousand thousand hellish window lights.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Here there is relative calm on the outskirts of Downtown, nothing more than a chill wind and stillness. As you approach LaFayette Towers, you can see that both balance precariously on a precipice that forms part of a massive crater that seems to encircle the heart of the city, cutting off roads and power lines like a god had taken a bite around this place with miles-wide jaws.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Standing below the East Tower, the structure that teeters and groans on the edge of the blast radius, you look up and see the copper frame buckle slightly in the wind, windows shimmering in Luna's light from high above. A tattered green awning hangs sloped above the entrance to this empty-looking building, but it is not unguarded. A doorman's long burgundy coat hangs disembodied as if worn by an invisible frame, a cap floating a little too close to the collar to accommodate a head. It hovers there, standing in eternal vigilance, the hem of its coat frayed and dirtied, but manages to look proud and official nonetheless. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The doors behind the watchman spirit hang haphazardly on their hinges, glossy black like obsidian, pitted and scored with age. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Above neon light flashes white and snaps from window to window, like arcs of static electricity.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> You go first, Jericho, padding down the stairs, claws clacking as they tick against rusty metal, two distinct scents rising above the others as you descend - heated stone, hot, baking embers. The light here is a low orange haze, like the glow from a stove fire or a steam engine. Indeed, you hear faint hisses echoing from somewhere far beyond, throttling with a burbling hiss through pipes overhead. All around you is tunnel, bundled pipes and corroded wire, making you feel like you were traveling through some kind of man-made blood vessel of concrete and iron. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The bottom of the stairs gives way to a five-foot gap, gnarled steel bundles spiking up from the ground like a tiger trap. It looks like a utility tunnel of some kind, fused with the dull brass roundness of boilers and valves, wire and thatched cable - all the trappings of a building in desperate need of attention. The walls are white but spotted with age, orange light sputtering from an open grate that licks flame but doesn't burn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Ahead, you see a mosaic of graffiti, tiles of colored, First Tongue runes that swirl into obscene designs that are vaguely urban, but somehow wholly alien.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">One after the other, you leap down, narrowly avoiding the sharp points of the accumulated debris below, deadly in its neglect. Open archways in the walls, half cluttered by moldy cardboard boxes and overturned shopping carts, reveal seething, burning machines, massive green-painted iron heaters that breathe in and out like they were alive, lungs ragged and hot. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The walls peel in places to reveal cold red brick the color of dried blood, infested with those maggot things, crawling and feeding as they grind the brick into meal. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You come to a single, innocuous-looking door that is tagged by graffiti that looks somewhat familiar. Yin's bold, artistic strokes and careful detail paints a mess of machinery and wires that swallows houses and buildings wholesale, a metal wolf with rust-colored plates for hide watching upon a lonely peak in the distance. It's as good a mark as any, though some of the paint bubbles and cracks at your approach. A knob with an old-style keyhole waits to be turned. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You can feel the tingle of the locus door as you near, prickling your hackles and making them stand on end.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As you near, Bastian, you can see that there are a pair of eyes, blank and metallic that are open upon the drawing, watching you from behind a tangle of nightmarish cable. You scent spirit above the usual haze of Hisil stench, like it were embedded there. Probably a lesser guardian aspect or some kind of alarum spirit.</span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div>Downtown Detroit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You emerge into a scene of holocaust. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In the Hisil, you had witnessed the alien devastation of Detroit's downtown from afar, but nothing had prepared you for what you saw here in the epicenter, at ground zero. The city looks like it has been razed by atomic fire, buildings bent by some ancient, massive blast wave that has melted surfaces together and fused the concrete under your feet to shards of razor-sharp, broken glass. The buildings are still burning here and there, though to the west you can see a massive firestorm sweeping the tallest buildings clean, scouring and devouring them to blackened, skeletal frames like a living, ravenous beast of hellish flame. There is no building untouched, no structure that is not gutted. Like the sprawling graveyard of blackened gods, the place is a labyrinth, all caved inwards along the slope of a massive crater. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Shadows are scarred permanently into the ground, of fleeing people with flailing limbs. Some still writhe against oozing blocks of scourged masonry, slime-dripping gutters that yawn open like mouths underfoot. Nearby you see an impaled, skeletal corpse that has bayonet blades for a spine, its lower jaw gone. It burns like it was doused in gasoline, quietly, pathetically moaning. The sky above is darkened with smoke from a hundred thousand such Armageddon corpse fires, obscuring Luna's face forever. Overhead it roils, circling and swirling like a hurricane storm, never raining but never abating.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Nightmarish desolation. It stinks of gun smoke, of blood, asphalt and dust. Fear and despair.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You realize that you can't move, your arms at your sides, looking from left to right, you find that you've stepped sideways into an open coffin standing nearly upright. Leaving, you see that your entry point was one of many others honeycombed into a wall of bloody brick and mortar behind you, like a blasphemous beehive, all of them moldy and rotten You see the other emerge a few feet away, from an identical coffin. The ground slopes down a hilly incline from where you stand, glass and sharp rebar poking up all around. On either side is a row of lavatories that look like they've been drenched in waste, stinking into the air, doors opening and shutting with thunderous, plastic anger.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A skeletal thing that looks like a cross between a dog and a broken-winged vulture tends to the box wall far above, no meat on its bones. It beats with a hammer and chisel incessantly, squawk-barking to itself. It caws irritably at your arrival and flaps away under the impossible power of its featherless limbs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Were that this place was dead. You can hear ghostly gunfire chattering all around, and as you get your bearings, a motorcycle spirit roars from the road up over to your left, leaping a low wall of broken rifle butts. Two nylon stocking masks float upon its back, fabric pressed against the impression of hateful, murderous features. The masks are disembodied and appear to belong to invisible frames wearing leather gangster jackets. Numina explodes from the sleeves like the staccato shots of an Uzi or Tech-9 as the terrifying group drive-bys the line of Port-A-Potties, riddling them with bulletholes, eliciting shrill, squeaking cries of agony. Bloody blue toilet fluid gushes out, and the things begin to shiver and grow dark as the motorcycle howls into the distance.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> It feels wrong. Not like a Wound, no - this place had been like this for so long that it was an open, blighted sore upon the Hisil. It was the </span></span><i>lil</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">, the spirit of this place, dying and corrupting everything around it. Certainly there were pockets of Wound here, maybe under your feet, for in the Urshul you felt faint tremors of massive machinery down below, of hollow earth and fiery industry, probably somehow feeding the corpse fires. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You look around, but besides the chill of the Hisil on this patch of high ground, you see no distinct threats waiting for you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The two of you descend the glassy, jagged slope, slipping on the bluish guts and blood of the dying lavatory things on either side, the doors opening proudly on the healthy ones, but haphazardly and sometimes not at all on the wounded or dead structures. Waiting for use. As you passed by, you see the toilet bowls shrivel into wrinkled mouths, growing teeth, suckling and snapping angrily as they are deprived of prey, these strange urban Venus mantraps.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You are careful not to cut yourselves on the ground, but despite your best efforts, Bastian, your paws are sliced up by errant shards of sharp atomic glass, the scent of his blood sharp in the foul air.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The two of you continue on through the strange, sprawling maze of crumpled streets and ruined city, the crocodile tooth leading you on a haphazard route that seems to be taking you in circles, but you realize you are only winding down and down the crater. You pass by sputtering neon signs in First Tongue, none of them making any sense, reflections of sales and failed commercialism, most of them leaking glowing blood onto the ground from on high. Shrieking numina snaps overhead like tracer rounds in an invisible spirit war, and more than once you need to duck your head to avoid being hit. When you look for who fired, you only see shadows flitting amongst the ruins. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You slide down slopes made from old car parts crunched up into a fine mulch, fused hubcaps rattling like mouths for you to save them, begging and pleading toothlessly in the First Tongue. Above, you hear the whine of rotors, and a patchwork blimp floats high overhead. It is made of what looks like air bladders of human flesh and faces with supports of giant bone, the back half clockwork engines and propellers. It is dangling with chains attached to the husks of derelict cars. A giant black screen is embedded across the side, scrolling glowing runes of First Tongue words.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">[THIS NIGHT ONLY]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">[EAT DRINK KILL ALL]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">[FATHER WOLF IS DEAD]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">[LONG LIVE THE HUZUR-KAR]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A blast of flame from a gutter a few yards to your right illuminates the last of the road ahead, broken off into darkness down below. The two of you stand on a flat ledge above a tunnel, looking down onto a blasted neighborhood that teeters on the edge of a vast chasm.<br /> </span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","user":"solidork","date":". 04-06-2016, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T04:10:01-07:00","id":863559,"title":"","content":"Also: <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://ih1.redbubble.net/image.57012544.5615/raf,750x1000,075,t,brown.u2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:52:34-07:00","id":864083,"title":"","content":"So spirits. Don't look 100% like the thing their a spirit of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:56:44-07:00","id":864085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vasilios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar?p=864083#post864083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So spirits. Don't look 100% like the thing their a spirit of?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that much was obvious, considering that they typically stop being spirits of just one thing once you get out of the lowest Ranks and several of them belong to categories whose purviews don't look like anything at all besides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:58:58-07:00","id":864088,"title":"","content":"It really didn't seem obvious